message: "If you use this study or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "Streets, Not Reputations: A Street-Level, Injury-Checked Cycling Risk Index for 300 European Cities"
authors:
  - family-names: Rotariu
    given-names: Victor
    affiliation: Defensive Pedal Research
type: report
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-20  # set to launch day
license: CC-BY-4.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22771452
url: "https://victorwho.github.io/european-cycling-risk-ranking/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/victorwho/european-cycling-risk-ranking"
keywords:
  - cycling safety
  - road safety
  - urban cycling
  - risk modelling
  - city ranking
  - OpenStreetMap
  - Europe
abstract: >-
  300 European cities in 31 countries ranked on the cycling risk of their
  street networks with one per-road risk model, aggregated into street risk,
  journey risk and low-stress access, with 90% rank intervals from 2,000
  method respecifications. In 18 cities with counter-measured exposure the
  index predicts serious-injury rates per passage; the association does not
  hold within countries. Preprint, open data supplement and ranking site.
